  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>The Nartuby runs through Draguignan, Trans-en-Provence and La Motte before joining the Argens, offering several waterfalls. A Himalayan suspension bridge, installed in 2021 (Var Tourisme, Dracénie Provence Verdon), spans the gorges at Trans-en-Provence, as part of the "Boucle panoramique du Calant": 1.6 km, about 40 minutes, easy with no elevation gain according to the town hall, starting from the village centre.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>Unlike the big Verdon lakes, the mood here is more intimate: the town hall describes the Nartuby as a torrential river carving gorges through the heart of the village. Neither the town nor the tourist office publishes any rule or swimming area for dogs: think of this place as a walk, not a swimming spot.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: the suspension bridge gives an impressive view of the water below — be careful if your dog isn't keen on heights.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>Lac de Carcès is about twenty minutes away to extend the freshwater outing.</p>
